Latest follow-up:

1. Labels such as `GAS TURBINE - BEARINGS` and `GAS TURBINE - CLEARANCES` map to `Gas Turbine` based on the leading phrase.
2. The rule applies only to the `COMPONENTS` section. It may be numbered `2. COMPONENTS` or `3. COMPONENTS`; do not assume a fixed section number. Reports without a Components section, including short reports, are assigned entirely to `shared`. All other sections are also `shared`.
3. Unlabeled content inside Components should use the easy path and remain `shared`. Some of this content may be text or scanned sub-reports. An `ambiguous` label with page fallback remains a possible future option, not part of the initial rule.
4. If Components is missing or cannot be detected, the whole document falls back to `shared`.
5. Validation should include the listed Gas Turbine, Steam Turbine, Generator, Uncategorized, sub-report, Components-as-section-3, and short-report examples from the latest review.

The initial label vocabulary is limited to Gas Turbine, Steam Turbine, Generator, and Uncategorized (`shared`).
